     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":0,\"rationale\":\"The target is an OR over four routes: vaultRead, shareMount, dbReplica and codeRepo. These rely on largely independent branches. shareMount is reached via backupHost, which can come from browserStore (via iotDevice or dmzWeb) or from dbLogin (dmzWeb AND memoryDump). vaultRead is reached via secretsManager, which needs monitoringHost AND fileServer (from ssoLogin). dbReplica and codeRepo are reached via serviceAccount, which needs ssoLogin AND vpnSession. Blocking ssoLogin cuts vaultRead, dbReplica and codeRepo, but shareMount stays reachable. Blocking dmzWeb still leaves browserStore reachable via iotDevice. No single step is common to every route, so there are no single points of failure.\"}"
    }
   ],
